# Waveform UI

Waveforms are measured data, not decoration.

Collection specimen marks are separate deterministic catalog identities derived from persisted take/source facts. They are not waveforms, audio fingerprints, quality scores, or random decorative waveform and must never replace or imitate PCM-derived peaks.

## Required

- Peaks from real PCM (worker min/max buckets); canvas renderer with `devicePixelRatio` scaling
- Clear zero axis and accurate time ruler; selection/edit boundaries aligned to time
- Preserve transients — no averaging away spikes; no exaggerated smoothing
- Mono: centered lane. Stereo: labeled L/R or explicit combined mode — never silent mono downmix
- Interactive handles may be DOM/SVG; waveform body stays canvas
- Trim grips hang below the wave frame (`--signal` block tabs); fade grips sit on the bottom edge of the time ruler (`--ink` wedge tabs) and stay anchored to retained start/end
- Fade visualization scales peaks by linear fade gain and draws a dashed `--ink` envelope diagonal (not signal)

## Forbidden

- Placeholder / random / asset waveforms after audio has loaded
- Uniform mirrored “blobs”, EQ bars, or stylized fake paths
- Animating the waveform shape unrelated to playback or input levels
- WebGL for MVP (not required)

Full spec: `briefing/04_WAVEFORM_AND_AUDIO_EDITOR.md`. Visual contract: `DESIGN.md`.
